# Smoke test for weather. Page 0 (the current-conditions panel)
# embeds a live clock label that ticks every render — fundamentally
# unsuitable for golden-image diff. So this scenario navigates to
# page 1 (`display_curve`, the 5-day forecast plot — no clock) via
# action TURN_RIGHT and screenshots there. The HTTP fixture chain
# (location search -> currentconditions -> forecast) has already
# populated run_data->wea by the time we get there, so the curve
# uses the canned daily_max/daily_min values.
#
# flash_seed pre-writes a config whose api_key is non-empty and not
# the WEATHER_API_KEY_PLACEHOLDER sentinel, so weather_api_key_configured()
# returns true and the fixture chain runs (without this seed, the new
# placeholder guard would short-circuit get_location_key and the curve
# panel would render with empty data — diff vs the golden).
# Six lines, matching write_config's emission order:
# api_key / city_name / location_key / weather_interval / time_interval / language

app weather
flash_seed /weather_accu.cfg "TEST_KEY\nBeijing\n\n900000\n900000\n0\n"

wait_ms 800
action TURN_RIGHT
wait_ms 200
screenshot 01_curve
assert_no_crash

action RETURN
wait_ms 200
assert_no_crash
